# Approved design library only

`design/registry.md` is the source of truth for allowed UI. Storybook (`packages/ui`) is the library.

## Building screens

- Use only components and patterns marked **Approved** in `design/registry.md`.
- Style only with design tokens: Tailwind utilities mapped in `packages/ui/src/styles/theme.css` or `var(--sgp-*)` from `design/tokens/tokens.css`. No raw hex colors, pixel font sizes, or one-off shadows.
- Exception: client data colors (status values, list values, conditional formatting) come from records at runtime, for example `statusValues` in `@sgp/mock-data`. Never hard-code status names, colors, or icons; render whatever the data says, legibly.
- Prototype screens live in `apps/prototype` and use data from `@sgp/mock-data`, never invented placeholder content. Read tables, fields, labels, and visibility through `resolveTableConfig`, and navigation through `buildNavTree`, so per-project configuration is respected.

```tsx
// Bad: raw values, invented component
<div style={{ background: '#1e1e1e', fontSize: 13 }}>...</div>

// Good: tokens via Tailwind utilities
<div className="bg-surface text-md text-fg">...</div>
```

## When something is missing

Do not improvise it inside a screen. Instead:

1. Build it in `packages/ui/src/` from existing tokens, with a story tagged `proposed`.
2. Add a row to `design/registry.md` with status **Proposed**.
3. Tell Nephi what it is, why it is needed, and which existing standards it follows.

## Approval

- Never mark anything **Approved** yourself. Only Nephi approves (the same no-self-approval rule the product enforces).
- After Nephi approves: change the story tag to `approved`, export it from `packages/ui/src/index.ts`, and record the date in the registry.
